cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite the archived Zenodo release below.
  No peer-reviewed version of this work has been published; the companion
  preprint listed under `identifiers` is a preprint only.
title: >-
  GatewayDB-MCP: A Configuration-Driven Bridge from JDBC Databases to MCP
  Tool Endpoints in Enterprise API Gateways
abstract: >-
  GatewayDB-MCP is an open-source Java framework that bridges JDBC-compatible
  relational databases to enterprise API gateway MCP proxies through XML
  property configuration alone, without custom application code. Bundled JDBC
  drivers cover MySQL, PostgreSQL, and SQL Server; MariaDB is available through
  an optional Maven profile. The framework uses a
  two-layer architecture in which the gateway layer supplies MCP protocol
  translation, OAuth 2.1, rate limiting, and OpenTelemetry audit using native
  gateway policies, while the bridge layer handles JDBC connectivity, schema
  introspection, query execution, SQL validation, and runtime generation of an
  x-mcp-tool-annotated OpenAPI 3.0.3 specification. Deployment modes are Apigee
  X embedded and a Docker sidecar compatible with Kong Gateway and Azure API
  Management. Known security limitations, including six documented SQL
  injection payloads that bypass the heuristic query validator, are described in
  the repository README and SECURITY.md.
